# Server Auth

## Authentication

- JWT tokens stored in http-only, secure, SameSite cookies — never in localStorage.
- Passwords hashed with `bcrypt` (minimum 12 rounds).
- Token refresh handled server-side; clients receive new cookies transparently.

## Authorization

- Protect endpoints with `@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)`.
- Role-based access via `@Roles('admin', 'editor')` decorator + `RolesGuard`.
- Access the authenticated user with `@CurrentUser()` parameter decorator.

## Example

```typescript
@Post('publish')
@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard, RolesGuard)
@Roles('editor', 'admin')
async publishSpec(@CurrentUser() user: AuthUser, @Param('id') id: string) {
  return this.specService.publish(id, user.id);
}
```

## Rules

- No secrets, tokens, or credentials in source code — use environment variables.
- Rate-limit auth endpoints (login, register, refresh) to prevent brute-force.
- Log authentication failures with context (IP, user agent) for audit.
- Invalidate tokens on password change.
